# Default text files use LF. Android scripts and patches retain their exact bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf
#
# This matters: Android's shell fails on CRLF line endings (a line that plainly
# exists reports "not found"), and a CRLF patch file will not apply. Marking these
# as binary stops Git from "helpfully" converting them on checkout for anyone who
# clones on Windows with core.autocrlf=true.
*.sh    -text
*.patch -text
*.prop  -text
*.py    -text
*.zip   -text
*.apk   -text
